Meet the Electro-Wick, a tiny, flexible strip embedded with a gradient of hydrophobic and super-hydrophilic nanomaterials. It works by applying a low-voltage electric field across its surface. When you place it between your teeth, the electric potential gradient drives water molecules and particulate matter to migrate rapidly along the strip, effectively 'scooping' debris away from the gum line. The geometry is a curved, V-shaped ribbon that conforms to the natural curvature of your molar, ensuring maximum contact area. The mechanism relies on dielectrophoresis and electro-osmosis, not mechanical friction. By reversing the polarity, you can flush debris into a collection reservoir at the end of the strip. This eliminates the need for physical scrubbing, reducing wear on your enamel while aggressively removing biofilm. It is a silent, electrically powered vacuum cleaner for your oral cavity, utilizing fundamental electromagnetic forces to achieve a level of cleanliness impossible with passive tools. It is efficient, quiet, and requires only a small battery pack for continuous operation. يُ
