Introducing the 'Resonant Vortex Scrubber.' This device utilizes a high-frequency piezoelectric transducer embedded in a flexible, ultrasonic tip that fits comfortably over your tooth. Instead of rigid bristles, the tip generates standing pressure waves in a sealed, viscous fluid-filled chamber. These waves create micro-jets of fluid that penetrate beneath dental plaque, utilizing cavitation bubbles to dislodge debris from the enamel surface without mechanical abrasion. The geometry is a conical nozzle that focuses these acoustic energy streams precisely at the gum line, where debris often accumulates. By tuning the frequency, you can select the intensity of the fluidic blast, ensuring gentle yet effective removal. The entire system operates wirelessly, powered by a small, rechargeable cell in the handle. It transforms the cleaning process from a physical scraping action into a precise, acoustic dissection, reducing the risk of enamel wear while achieving deep-cleaning results in seconds. This approach leverages fluid dynamics and wave physics to achieve a level of precision unattainable by manual tools, making it ideal for users seeking a non-invasive, high-efficiency oral care solution.วัฒนธรรม
