Presenting the 'Magnetophoretic Lattice,' a paradigm shift in oral hygiene that abandons mechanical contact entirely. This tool features a dense array of sub-micron neodymium magnets arranged in a complex, 3D lattice structure that lines the inner surface of a custom-fitted oral retainer. When powered by a low-voltage electromagnetic field, these micro-magnets induce precise magnetic forces on ferromagnetic nanoparticles suspended in a biocompatible, magnetorheological fluid. As the user moves their jaw, the shifting magnetic fields create dynamic shear stresses within the fluid, generating a localized, high-velocity flow that strips away biofilm and debris from the tooth surface. The geometry is designed to match the natural contours of the dental arch, ensuring that every nook and cranny is reached without manual dexterity. This method leverages the unique property of magnetorheological fluids to change viscosity instantaneously in response to magnetic fields, allowing for controlled, high-intensity cleaning without the risk of abrasive wear. It is a silent, vibration-free process that uses magnetic force to manipulate matter at the microscopic level, offering a level of cleanliness that traditional tools simply cannot achieve. This is not just cleaning; it is magnetic manipulation of biological material.เป็นผู้
